WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.880
A park at dusk.

2
00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:03.710
The light is fading.

3
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:08.280
A young soldier, back from the
war: "He sat in a wheeled chair,

4
00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.740
waiting for dark," Then
the poem cuts away.

5
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.260
Evenings in town.

6
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.670
A football crowd carrying
a player shoulder-high.

7
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.010
A recruiting table.

8
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.450
A band playing.

9
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.710
And then, just as suddenly,
back to the chair.

10
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.660
Again and again, the poem cuts back.

11
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.410
So why does it keep jumping
between then and now?

12
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.740
In this mission, you'll meet Owen in 1917,

13
00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:36.260
invalided home and writing
at Craiglockhart hospital.

14
00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:39.740
You'll map the poem's moments
in the order Owen gives them.

15
00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:44.910
And you'll spot the small word
that pulls him back each time: Now.

16
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.150
Your mission: explain why the poem
keeps jumping between then and now.
